r-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335368" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\text{L1}"] ["math" "\\text{L2}"] ["math" "\\text{L4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335368" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{L4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335368" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335368" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the absorption property"] ["text" "the constant multiple property"] ["text" "the reflexive property"] ["text" "the sum property"] ["text" "the transitive property"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335368" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the constant multiple property"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following statement. \n\nIf $f(x)={e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x},$ then $f=O(1)$ as $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nA proof of the statement is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,f=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=O\\,({e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,f=O({e}^{-x})$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,{e}^{-x}=O(1)$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(1)$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from lines \n{{field-4}} and \n{{field-5}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property. \n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If \n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\n \nthen \n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\nf=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nand this is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L3}.$ From line $\\text{L1},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=O\\,({e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L2}$ and $\\text{the absorption property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O\\,({e}^{-2x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{e}^{-x})=O\\,({e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line $\\text{L3},$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O({e}^{-x})\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L4},$ we have\n\n$$\n{e}^{-x}=O(1).\n$$\n\nThus,  by lines $\\text{L3 and L4}$ and $\\text{the transitive property},$ we have \n\n$$\nf=O(1).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335468" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5a77a02899114e11f4cbd602681801cbe4c7c18620366c8753387bf5187d3966"} {"question" "q-335468" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14066660/state.json" "file_sha256" "de476451e29fa550ded171a5fc46c2eb212b825051bf926f91afe5bd15b258fd"} {"question" "q-335468" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/ch